        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">WebCrytpo supports EC compressed points in FF145 in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1971499\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1971499</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">More specifically, I think \"support\" means \"can import keys defined as such points\" - am checking.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds a release note and comment in body of docs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3607703023\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41870\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41870/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41870\">#41870</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">NOTE, first commit is a layout change only - so you can review actual changes just by looking at the second commit</p>",
